{
	"_readme": [
		"Every row on the Options page about how the game plays, pressed through real keys from both",
		"ways in (M51). At the title each play row is pressed twice, which is there and back again,",
		"because each offers two values. Mid-run, from the pause menu, Movement is turned to Tiles and",
		"then Saving to save points - and the one tap south after the first is a whole tile, which is",
		"what proves the choice reached the player rather than only the page.",
		"A --qa-script run empties its settings file at boot, so every choice here starts from nothing."
	],
